{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"The level-9 entry reproduces as a 6-pixel lattice with four movable bridges, two pegs, and one carrier. A static peg-solitaire abstraction reduces it to one peg on the carrier but does not reward the level—the last move causes a large scene transition instead. That confirms the puzzle has a second wrapped phase, so I’m now tracing the candidate route by symbolic stage states rather than treating the first board as the whole goal."}}
